# THE DATA LEMMA, STRING HALF (SPEC.md §5.2; issue #133): a data property whose
# only uses are string literals on named individuals, and whose ranges hold
# them, is string-asserted, and its assertions and ranges are inert in every
# rung. :v is asserted "x" (plain) with range xsd:string, and :w is asserted
# "y"@en with range rdfs:Literal. Both hold, so both are inert, and nothing is
# omitted. :A and :B are disjoint and :D is unrelated to them, so the verdict
# is COHERENT (exit 0). Before the fix, each assertion was an omission and
# every probe answered unknown; now a probe about :D's unrelated class answers no.

@prefix :     <https://example.org/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:A owl:disjointWith :B .
:v a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
:w a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range rdfs:Literal .
:j a :D ; :v "x" .
:k a :D ; :w "y"@en .
